## Reference recording and tests
Executed, read-only reference tree, output only inside this task worktree:
node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-stats.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --out native/core/fixtures/office-stats/golden.json
3,226 cases. The recorder rejects a package version other than 4.6.1.
Golden outcomes compare f64 bits (including signed zero/NaN), errors, exception
messages, arrays, undefined/null and dates. Cases include missing arguments,
empty/nested/mixed arrays, numeric strings, whitespace, dates, booleans, multiple
errors, nonfinite values, unequal paired ranges, ties, criterion wildcards,
percentile/rank boundaries, and V8 sorting runs over 64 entries.

Main test: every_descriptive_result_equals_the_recording_bit_for_bit
Ignored opt-in reference recorder: twin_live_stats
Initially ignored hot-registration gate: descriptive_functions_are_registered_in_the_production_library

The source deliberately retains odd installed-library behavior: SMALL with bad k
returns its parsed array; TRIMMEAN with zero trim removes one item per end;
MODE.SNGL can throw on a second parse; AVERAGEIFS throws on an error-valued
applyCriteria result whereas MAXIFS/MINIFS return infinity of the relevant sign.
No textbook validation or precision tolerance was substituted.

## Remaining acceptance work (not executed by implementer)
No cargo, build, Rust tests, apps, commits or dependency downloads were run.
A rustfmt pass parsed/formatted the new Rust source; this is not a typecheck.
Lead must run offline check/clippy and the twin test, resolve any mismatch,
then apply registration and run the production gate. Exact NaN/sign behavior
is intentionally asserted, not waived. Integration is not declared verified.

PERMUT uses the same ascending factorial products, stopping arithmetic once
171 yields infinity. It avoids Node's incidental native-stack exhaustion for
very large finite positive factorial arguments; negative/infinite nonterminating
arguments retain the thrown message. The fixture is bounded to factorial 1000;
no claim is made about reproducing Node's version/cache-dependent stack threshold.
The four-library engine gate remains incomplete until the other tasks land.

Lead correction: LOGEST reparses both numeric arrays through LINEST, including NaN x; non-progressing positive factorial recursion (n - 1 == n) retains Node's thrown error. Three new Node cases record these paths.
